<title>HONG KONG: Korea Exchange Bank seen planning FRN.</title>
<headline>Korea Exchange Bank seen planning FRN.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Korea Exchange Bank is planning a US$200 million floating rate note issue, bankers said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>They said the facility has a final maturity of one year.</p>
<p>It will be issued off the bank's US$4 billion Euro Medium Term Note Programme.</p>
<p>A mandate is to be awarded soon, bankers noted.</p>
<p>An issue specific rating will be sought.</p>
<p>The issuer's long-term senior debt and deposits are rated Baa1 by Moody's Investors Service.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2847 4039  http://www.hk97.com</p>
